"""Belém: the rising of 14 April 1823.  A sample game for the Grognard
engine.

Brazil has declared its independence, but Grão-Pará still answers to
Lisbon.  On the night of 13 April a hundred conspirators meet at João
Baptista Balbi's house in Belém; at dawn they take the artillery park,
send up rockets, and march to the Largo das Mercês to proclaim Dom Pedro.
Will the regiments come out for them, or for the governor?  Play either
side against the computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./belem (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is saved
to ~/.belem.json.  ./belem --selftest checks the map and plays a game
between two computer players.
"""

